{
  "id": "stress",
  "title": "Stress",
  "description": "Calculate normal stress and shear stress. Stress is the ratio between applied force and cross-sectional area where the applied force is acting.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Stress Calculator\n\nCalculate **Normal Stress** and **Shear Stress** based on applied forces and cross-sectional area.\n\n### Normal Stress\nNormal stress (σ) = FN / A, where FN is the normal force perpendicular to the area.\n\n### Shear Stress\nShear stress (τ) = FV / A, where FV is the shear force in the plane of the area."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "force",
          "label": "Applied Force",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "N",
          "defaultValue": 10000
        },
        {
          "id": "area",
          "label": "Cross-sectional Area",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m²",
          "defaultValue": 0.00203
        },
        {
          "id": "forceType",
          "label": "Force Type",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Normal Force",
              "value": "normal"
            },
            {
              "label": "Shear Force",
              "value": "shear"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "normal"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "stress",
          "label": "Stress",
          "formula": "inputs.force / inputs.area",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "stressMPa",
          "label": "Stress (MPa)",
          "formula": "(inputs.force / inputs.area) / 1000000",
          "unit": "MPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}